NNAAMMEE
       zgrep - search possibly compressed files for a regular expression

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       zzggrreepp [ grep_options ] [[ --ee ]] _p_a_t_t_e_r_n _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e...

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The zzggrreepp command invokes ggrreepp on compressed or gzipped files.  All op‐
       tions specified are passed directly to ggrreepp.  If no file is  specified,
       then  the  standard input is decompressed if necessary and fed to grep.
       Otherwise the given files are uncompressed  if  necessary  and  fed  to
       ggrreepp.

       If the GREP environment variable is set, zzggrreepp uses it as the ggrreepp pro‐
       gram to be invoked.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
       Exit status is 0 for a match, 1 for no matches, and 2 if trouble.

BBUUGGSS
       The following ggrreepp options are not  supported:  ----ddeerreeffeerreennccee--rreeccuurrssiivvee
       (--RR),  ----ddiirreeccttoorriieess  (--dd),  ----eexxcclluuddee,  ----eexxcclluuddee--ffrroomm, ----eexxcclluuddee--ddiirr,
       ----iinncclluuddee, ----nnuullll (--ZZ), ----nnuullll--ddaattaa (--zz), and ----rreeccuurrssiivvee (--rr).

